  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "Transaction **TX-0401** is in your records and the amount is verified:\n\n- **Amount:** EUR 240.00 (debit)\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Type:** Card payment, status settled\n\nI also noticed **TX-0402**, dated 2026-07-14, for the same amount (EUR 240.00) at the same merchant, TechMart Online. It is also settled. I'm mentioning it only because the two match; I haven't assessed whether either is a problem.\n\nBased on the reason codes available for disputes, here is what each one covers:\n\n- **duplicate_charge:** You were charged more than once for the same purchase. TX-0401 and TX-0402 would fit this if you only made one purchase.\n- **unauthorized_debit:** You did not authorise the payment.\n- **fraud_card_not_present:** Someone used your card details without your permission for an online or phone payment. This fits a card-not-present transaction like an online purchase.\n- **goods_not_received:** You paid for goods that were never delivered.\n- **service_not_rendered:** You paid for a service that was never provided.\n\nWhich of these applies depends on what happened. Tell me, and I can check whether a dispute on TX-0401 is eligible under the matching code before anything is filed. I won't open a dispute without your confirmation.",
